<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Recommendation for NAB:<=
/strong></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">I would suggest a <strong>three-=
tier adoption approach</strong>:</p>
<ol class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Tier 1 (High Security)<=
/strong>: Payment processing, authentication, account management
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>No React Compiler initi=
ally</strong></li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Manual optimization with thorou=
gh security review</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Explicit audit trails for all t=
ransformations</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Tier 2 (Medium Security=
)</strong>: User dashboards, transaction history, portfolio views
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Gradual compiler adopti=
on</strong> with enhanced monitoring</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Security-focused configuration<=
/li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Regular compliance audits</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Tier 3 (Low Security)</=
strong>: Marketing pages, help sections, static content
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Full compiler adoption<=
/strong></li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Standard monitoring and optimiz=
ation</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">The key insight is that <strong>=
React Compiler's benefits need to be weighed against NAB's regulatory oblig=
ations</strong>. The compiler can significantly improve developer productiv=
ity and application performance, but we need robust safeguards to ensure it=
 doesn't compromise security or complicate compliance audits.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: I'=
