<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>5. Where React Compiler =
Helps vs. Hurts:</strong></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Helps:</strong></p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Automatic memoization</=
strong> of expensive calculations (portfolio metrics, price formatting)</li=
>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Stable callbacks</stron=
g> for event handlers without manual useCallback</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Reduced bundle size</st=
rong> from removing manual memoization code</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Consistent optimization=
</strong> across all components</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Potential Issues:</stron=
g></p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Predictability</strong>=
: In high-frequency scenarios, we need <strong>deterministic performance</s=
trong></li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Memory usage</strong>: =
Compiler might memoize too aggressively, holding onto data longer than nece=
ssary</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Debugging</strong>: Har=
der to profile and debug performance issues in generated code</li>
</ul>
