<ol class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>React Query</strong> ha=
ndles the <strong>"what data"</strong> (fetching, caching, synchronization)=
</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>React Compiler</strong>=
 handles the <strong>"how to render"</strong> (memoization, re-render optim=
ization)</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Together</strong>: They=
 create a <strong>highly efficient data-to-UI pipeline</strong></li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Best Practices:</strong>=
</p>
<ol class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Let React Query manage =
server state</strong> - don't try to memoize API responses manually</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Let React Compiler opti=
mize derived calculations</strong> - don't manually memoize transforms of q=
uery data</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Coordinate invalidation=
</strong> between both systems for consistency</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Monitor both layers</st=
rong> to understand where performance bottlenecks occur</li>
</ol>
