<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">This <strong>layered approach</s=
trong> gives us the best of both worlds: robust server state management wit=
h React Query and automatic component optimization with React Compiler, cre=
ating a highly performant and maintainable architecture for NAB's complex f=
inancial dashboards.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Ex=
cellent! Your solution demonstrates a sophisticated understanding of how th=
ese modern React tools work together. I'm particularly impressed by your co=
nsideration of edge cases like connection drops and multi-tab consistency -=
 those are exactly the kinds of real-world issues we face at NAB.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Let me ask you one final technic=
al question before we wrap up: You've built this dashboard with React Compi=
ler optimization in mind. How would you <strong>test</strong> this applicat=
ion? Specifically, how do you test components that are optimized by React C=
ompiler, and how do you validate that the compiler optimizations are actual=
ly working as expected without breaking your testing strategy?</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Candidate</strong>: <str=
ong>Excellent final question!</strong> Testing React Compiler-optimized app=
lications requires a <strong>multi-layered testing strategy</strong> that v=
alidates both functionality and performance characteristics. This is partic=
ularly critical in financial services where we need to ensure that compiler=
 optimizations don't introduce subtle bugs.</p>
